"/* tokens/dark-arm-glass.css
   The .dark arm of the DEEP tier. The calm ladder has no dark arm any more: its
   saturate is one mode-invariant value and its radii are one set, so a dark
   re-declaration of the composed rungs would be five copies of the light recipe.
   What differs in dark is the INK, and that is one line in tokens/dark-arm.css.
   Its own .dark block, @import-ed by tokens.css IMMEDIATELY AFTER dark-arm.css. */

/* THE DARK DEEP ARM HAD NEVER PAINTED — ANYWHERE, IN EITHER DIRECTION.

   It used to be declared on the bare `.dark` root, and it read
   `--glass-blur-deep-active-radius`, which is declared ONLY on `.glass-deep`
   (deliberately: the LERP eager-substitutes `--glass-depth` at its declaring
   element, so at `:root` the grade freezes at the initial value 1 and every
   deep surface paints the ceiling). Off a deep surface the composite was
   therefore guaranteed-INVALID; on one, `.glass-deep`'s own element-level
   declaration beat the root by inheritance. Two exits, no paint.

   The cure is to declare the arm WHERE ITS INPUTS LIVE: on `.glass-deep` under a
   plain `.dark` ancestor (never `:global()` in a scoped block, never inside
   `light-dark()`). The radius stays the SAME LERP — radius-only across modes;
   what dark changes is that saturate holds at the named ceiling
   (`--glass-saturate-deep`) instead of at a point part-way up the light arm's
   lerp. One consumer write to that token still retunes both modes. */
@layer components {
    .dark .glass-deep {
        --glass-blur-deep:
            blur(var(--glass-blur-deep-active-radius))
            saturate(var(--glass-saturate-deep));
    }
}

