   for non-supporting engines). The pure `var()`-alias re-declarations
   (`--muted`/`--secondary`/`--accent`/`--border`/`--input`/… and the
   `--background`/`*-foreground` aliases) are DELETED — they auto-track the
   `--neutral-*` ladder + `--foreground` resolved above; only EXPLICIT-color
   dark values (and the non-color overrides §2d) stay.

   IDIOM-REVERSAL — one mechanism per
   token TYPE. COLOR tokens: light-dark.css is the CANONICAL single source; the
   `.dark {}` color values below are the fallback-floor LOCKSTEP WITNESSES —
   they MUST byte-agree with the light-dark() dark arg, never a second value
   (`proof:glass` clause DA1 reds a divergence). SHADOW / INSET /
